NUM-46: book the mass left in a dried-out node or link once, not twice

qualrout.c books the pollutant mass left in a conduit or storage unit when
it dries with massbal_addToFinalStorage(). It went into
StepQualTotals[p].finalStorage, which massbal_updateRoutingTotals() adds to
the run total with no time-step factor; that function runs at the end of
step n and again at the start of step n+1 before the step totals are
cleared, so the residue was counted twice. Add it to the run total
(QualTotals) directly; StepQualTotals.finalStorage then stays zero.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-46_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/massbal.c b/src/legacy/engine/massbal.c
index 80bb10e..7111e35 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/massbal.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/massbal.c
@@ -517,7 +517,9 @@ void massbal_addSeepageLoss(int pollutIndex, double w)
 void massbal_addToFinalStorage(int pollutIndex, double w)
 {
     if ( pollutIndex < 0 || pollutIndex >= Nobjects[POLLUT] ) return;
-    StepQualTotals[pollutIndex].finalStorage += w;
+    // --- w is a mass, not a rate: book it once in the run total
+    //     (massbal_updateRoutingTotals runs twice per step's totals)
+    QualTotals[pollutIndex].finalStorage += w;
 }
 
